_refine.details                                  
;Residues simultaneously refined in two or more conformations are:
Thr26, Val31, Ser49, Gln50, Val53, Leu67, Met104, Ser110, Ser116, Lys224, Ser236.

Note that HOH383 makes short H-bonds to OgSer195 and O6' of the inhibitor
Disordered waters are: 
HOH335 which is close to HOH336;
HOH345 which is close to HOH346;
HOH381 which is close to HOH382;
HOH417 which is close to HOH418;
HOH431 which is close to HOH432;
HOH509 which is close to HOH510;
HOH511 which is close to HOH512;
HOH513 which is close to HOH514;
HOH513 which is close to a symmetry-related equivalent of HOH528;
HOH535 which is close to HOH536;

HIS91 is MONOPROTONATED ON THE EPSILON NITROGEN.
His57 is doubly protonatd.
;
